WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.092
This slide focuses on Patient-age list management
Start with what the structure represents

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:11.905
then connect that idea to the example on the slide
Lists are useful when

00:00:11.931 --> 00:00:17.513
a collection grows as new records arrive Add and
summarize generic patient ages

00:00:19.363 --> 00:00:24.984
Before running the code predict the output Run the
example in the browser inspect

00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:30.628
the result then change one item index or value and
run it again Notice which

00:00:30.655 --> 00:00:34.128
operations change the original list and which simply
read from it
